    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>style=plain
fontsize=18
Service FSM (Ebene 1) — ServiceState + ServiceCalibSubStates (Implementierung Team 3-3)</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>

  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>20</x>
      <y>620</y>
      <w>1100</w>
      <h>120</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>fontsize=11
Legende / Abweichung zur alten UML
--
• Einstieg: IdleState oder ReadyForServiceState — START lang → ServiceState
• Abbruch: STOP_RELEASED → IdleState | ConnectionLost: ServiceCalibRegistry speichert Phase → Resume
• Entfernt (alt): WP_2, adjust_wp, Back_to_Entry, driveLeft, Start_Tick_measuring
• Neu: getrennte Wait-Zustaende je Messsegment | Slow endet CHUTE | Normal endet END | Speichern erst nach Wait_Wp_Removed + RESET_RELEASED
• Anlage 1 (Weiche): Slow → Rutsche (CHUTE) | Normal → Weiche offen bis END
• Anlage 2 (Auswerfer): pushEjector 1s bei EJECTOR_BLOCKED (Slow) | Normal bis END</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>

  <!-- ServiceState Composite -->
  <element>
    <id>UMLState</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>20</x>
      <y>50</y>
      <w>1060</w>
      <h>550</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>ServiceState
symbol=composite
valign=top
fontsize=14
--
Composite: leitet Events an aktuellen Sub-State (m_sub)
entry: applyServiceEntry() | exit: applyServiceExit()
STOP_RELEASED → IdleState</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>

